jobs.description:
As an E&I Maintenance Technician, you will be responsible for maintaining, installing, and troubleshooting electrical and instrumentation systems within industrial plants. You will work with control systems, sensors, measuring equipment, and electrical installations to keep industrial processes running smoothly.

Your responsibilities include:

- Installing and connecting instrumentation and electrical systems;
- Testing, calibrating, and commissioning measuring instruments;
- Performing preventive and corrective maintenance activities;
- Troubleshooting faults in electrical and control systems;
- Ensuring all work complies with safety standards and regulations, including ATEX guidelines.
- You will work independently as well as together with colleagues on industrial projects and maintenance operations.

- MBO level 3 or 4 in Electrical Engineering, Instrumentation, Mechatronics, or similar;
- Experience with E&I systems in industrial environments;
- Knowledge of NEN 3140 and preferably ATEX;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B;
- Accurate, proactive, and solution-oriented mindset;
- Good communication skills in Dutch or English.

Are you an enthusiastic Order Picker with EPT experience, or are you eager to learn? We are looking for motivated candidates to join a modern logistics company in Helmond. As an Order Picker with EPT, you will be responsible for collecting, checking, and moving goods throughout the warehouse. Your work ensures that customer orders are processed accurately and shipped on time.

Your responsibilities:

- Picking customer orders using a handheld scanner;
- Checking orders before shipment;
- Moving goods and pallets using an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT);
- Wrapping, labeling, and scanning pallets;
- Performing Value Added Services (VAS) activities;
- Supporting various warehouse and logistics processes;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized working environment.

Working Hours in the regular day shift: 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule applies:

- 06:00 AM – 03:00 PM
- 03:00 PM – 12:00 AM

- Has experience operating an EPT or is willing to learn;
- Fulltime available;
- Is flexible regarding tasks and working hours;
- Performs well under pressure;
- Enjoys working in a team;
- Has a good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Has a proactive and hands-on attitude.

Are You Our New Kitchen Steward?Are you hardworking, detail-oriented and proud of creating a clean and organised workplace? Then you could be the Kitchen Steward we are looking for at Hilton Garden Inn Leiden. We are looking for a part-time Steward for 24 hours a week! As a Kitchen Steward, you ensure that all dishes, kitchen utensils and equipment used by our Food & Beverage operation are cleaned thoroughly and ready for use. You work early and/or late shifts in the kitchen and stewarding area and collaborate closely with the Kitchen and Food & Beverage teams.What will you be doing?&middot;        Working with the team to create an excellent guest experience&middot;        Cleaning and correctly storing dishes, kitchen utensils and equipment&middot;        Keeping the stewarding area clean, safe and organised&middot;        Polishing and sorting cutlery, glassware and crockery&middot;        Using cleaning materials and equipment safely and responsibly&middot;        Following hygiene, food safety and health and safety standards&middot;        Supporting the Kitchen and Food & Beverage teams whenever needed

